What are ATP Test Swabs?
ATP test swabs are specialized hygiene monitoring tools designed to detect adenosine triphosphate (ATP)—the universal energy molecule found in all living cells. These disposable swabs use bioluminescence technology to measure organic residues on surfaces, providing rapid cleanliness verification in food processing, healthcare facilities, and pharmaceutical manufacturing. When combined with luminometers, they deliver quantitative hygiene data in relative light units (RLUs), enabling compliance with sanitation protocols.
Marketed by leading manufacturers like Neogen (3M) and Hygiena, ATP test swabs are essential tools for real-time hygiene validation. They are widely adopted across North America, Europe, and Asia-Pacific, with the surface ATP test segment currently dominating market share due to its versatile applications.
